  "notes": "S077 Industrial Basin BA combined field (Windows W29 2026-11-19): sibling of S074 with the identical measured layout (same anchors, pads, instance pads and routes, so the authored layout frame is the same as S074's). Air profile: helipads and helicopters only, no Airport and no fixed-wing aircraft (owner's S004 decision applied by the program lead; Airport-only dump on this source: 62 tested, 0 valid). The AirReturn helipad pads are the S074 ones. S074 notes follow. S074 Industrial Basin BA ground established (Windows W29 2026-11-19). Measured from the S074 stride-8 layout dump (win-dev-unity w29-dump-S074-stride8; host = S074 provisional bootstrap, program lead option 1). Every building pad centre is a native-validated unrotated dump candidate centre (codex notes w29_pick_layout.py; the starting-grant placer does not rotate, 6 m inside the playable bounds); instance pads follow the compiler's per-kind order (Supply: oil pump, refinery, fuel bladder, fabrication depot, refinery module; Service: watchtower, approach watchtower, satellite dish). Spawn and rally pads sit on passable level blocks on the nearest level passable blocks to each base inside its own half (player z>=545, enemy z<530) (enemy spawn pads on the level patch east of x 895); route waypoints are passable blocks with straight passable segments to both stagings. Player base on the level north cluster; enemy base in the south on not-level ground, which the native validator accepts; the level patch east of x 895 is kept for the enemy spawn and rally pads. S073's deployment anchors (800,600 / 930,470) only seeded the search. No legal Airport site on this source (Airport-only dump: 62 tested, 0 valid). Player spawn and rally pads moved onto the S073 player deployment anchor (800,600), where the legacy S073 starts its units: at (816,575.5) the second player rifleman could not spawn (w29-s074-c, BlockedSpawn) although the bitmap there is clear. Spawn and rally pads re-chosen from the decoded map surface (Assets/Game/Data/MapSurfaces/Match_Map_MapSurfaceData.asset, offline read-only, codex notes w29_surface.py / w29_pad_surface.py): every cell of each pad plus a 1 m margin passes MapSurfaceTraversalValidation (infantry pads: infantry bit and slope <= 35 deg or road; vehicle and rally pads: vehicle bits and slope <= 18 deg or road), clear of the placed buildings by 3 m, and each spawn pad holds at least two passable layout-bitmap blocks (pad_preflight rule). The earlier infantry pads had 13/120 (816,575.5) and 0/120 (800,600) infantry-admitted cells: a north-west strip (about x 740-808, z 552-660) is not traversable although the layout bitmap shows it clear.",
